 "caveats": [
  "Glen Canyon uses a measured sub-daily gage. Hoover does not exist at sub-daily resolution publicly, so its intraday shape is synthetic load-following fitted to real daily volumes.",
  "Headroom is nameplate minus hydro output, which is PHYSICAL headroom and not available transfer capability. See the WAPA note in fpv_forward_mc.py. Every curtailment figure here is an upper bound on what could actually be delivered.",
  "Hoover's q_at_cap and minimum flows are approximate.",
  "PVGIS is UTC and USGS is local standard time. The solar series is shifted by 7 hours before alignment. An earlier run without this shift reported a positive solar-hydro correlation, which was an artifact.",
  "Solar is held at the 2015 irradiance year across all release years, both because PVGIS-NSRDB coverage ends there and because it isolates hydrology as the variable under test."
 ]
}